Included in the source tree and in the wheel
--------------------------------------------
* PropBank frames annex: src/memory_kernel/data/propbank-frames-annex/. Framesets in PropBank format, eight of them
  adaptations of PropBank framesets. Licensed under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
  (CC BY-SA 4.0); the Apache-2.0 licence does not apply to this directory. The directory has its own LICENSE and NOTICE,
  which name the upstream work, state the changes and give the attribution.
* English stopword list: src/memory_kernel/data/english_stopwords.json is a snapshot of the NLTK English stopwords corpus
  (198 terms), taken with NLTK 3.9.1. The corpus README says the lists "were obtained from:
  http://anoncvs.postgresql.org/cvsweb.cgi/pgsql/src/backend/snowball/stopwords/" and that "The English list has been
  augmented" (https://github.com/nltk/nltk_data/issues/22). The nltk_data project lists the corpus among the datasets
  whose licence is unclarified.

Fetched by `mk setup` and not redistributed here
------------------------------------------------
Each item keeps the licence its distributor gives it. Nothing below is copied into this repository or its wheel.
* PropBank frames (upstream), CC BY-SA 4.0, https://github.com/propbank/propbank-frames at commit
  c66e0ccf28b53f00051b187db83e937b5bee2e32.
* FCG Go engine binary and its grammar image (pb-en-no-single-role-frames.fci), fetched through the pyfcg package from the
  FCG Go distribution at emergent-languages.org. They are fetched at setup and never redistributed by this project; their
  terms are those of their distributor.
* en_core_web_sm 3.8.0 (spaCy English pipeline, MIT; its LICENSES_SOURCES lists OntoNotes 5, ClearNLP and WordNet 3.0), the
  NLTK WordNet 3.0 corpus (Princeton University licence, Copyright 2006 Princeton University) and the tiktoken
  cl100k_base file.
* benepar_en3 (Berkeley Neural Parser English model), from the benepar GitHub release page, used by the optional
  `[parser]` extra. The release states no licence. The model is based on T5-small (Apache-2.0 per its model card) and was
  trained on the Penn Treebank Revised (LDC2015T13), which is distributed under the LDC User Agreement. Check these terms
  before you redistribute the model or anything that includes it.

